data: {"text":"1. That the Applicant seeks regular bail in connection with FIR No. 124/2026 dated 15."}

data: {"text":"03.2026, registered at Police Station Kotwali, under Sections 303 and 351 of the Bharatiya Nyaya Sanhita, 2023, wherein"}

data: {"text":" the Applicant has been falsely implicated by the Opposite Party.\n\n2. That the facts giving rise to the present FIR are that"}

data: {"text":" the Applicant has been falsely implicated in the aforementioned FIR due to a land dispute with the complainant. The entire case"}

data: {"text":" against the Applicant is based on false and fabricated allegations made with malicious intent to har"}

data: {"text":"ass and implicate the Applicant in a criminal case.\n\n3. That the Applicant submits that he was not present at the time and"}

data: {"text":" place of the alleged incident and has credible witnesses who can establish his alibi. The Applicant was"}

data: {"text":" elsewhere at the time when the alleged offence is said to have been committed,"}

data: {"text":" and this fact can be substantiated through reliable evidence and witness testimony"}

data: {"text":".\n\n4. That the Applicant was arrested on 16.03.2026 and has been languishing in judicial custody since then without any justifiable reason. The continued"}

data: {"text":" detention of the Applicant is causing irreparable hardship and violates his fundamental right to life and liberty guaranteed under"}

data: {"text":" Article 21 of the Constitution of India.\n\n5. That the Applicant has been falsely implicated in the present case due to the existing land dispute with the complainant. The"}

data: {"text":" complainant, having failed to succeed in civil proceedings, has now resorted to filing"}

data: {"text":" false criminal complaints to pressurize and harass the Applicant. The allegations made against"}

data: {"text":" the Applicant are entirely baseless and without any merit.\n\n6. That the Applicant is a respectable member of society with deep"}

data: {"text":" roots in the community and has no intention or inclination to flee from justice. He"}

data: {"text":" has been residing at the same address for several years and has strong family"}

data: {"text":" and social ties that ensure his presence during the trial proceedings.\n\n7. That the Applicant has no"}

data: {"text":" criminal antecedents whatsoever and has never been involved in any criminal activity in the past. His character and conduct have always been exemplary, and there"}

data: {"text":" is nothing on record to suggest that he would misuse his liberty if granted"}

data: {"text":" bail.\n\n8. That the Applicant undertakes to cooperate fully with the investigation and trial proceedings. He shall remain present"}

data: {"text":" before the investigating agency and the Court as and when required and"}

data: {"text":" shall not tamper with any evidence or influence any witnesses in the case.\n\n9. That Section"}

data: {"text":" 351 of BNS, 2023 under which the Applicant is charged is a bailable offence, and the Applicant is entitled"}

data: {"text":" to bail as a matter of right. Even in respect of Section"}

data: {"text":" 303 of BNS, 2023, which is non-bailable, the circumstances of the present case warrant the grant of bail in"}

data: {"text":" favour of the Applicant.\n\n10. That the investigation in the matter is pending, and there"}

data: {"text":" is no likelihood of the same being completed in the near future. The continued detention of the Applicant serves no useful"}

data: {"text":" purpose and would only result in unnecessary harassment and violation of his fundamental rights without any corresponding benefit to the cause of justice."}

